==","user":{"login":"asottile","id":1810591,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MTA1OTE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1810591?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/asottile","html_url":"https://github.com/asottile","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asottile/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asottile/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asottile/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asottile/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asottile/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asottile/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asottile/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asottile/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asottile/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-04-03T02:23:05Z","updated_at":"2021-04-03T02:23:05Z","body":"In GitLab by @sigmavirus24 on Aug 23, 2016, 07:07\n\nIf they're exporting them, why not add them to `__all__`, e.g.,\n\n```py\n__all__ = (\n    'ObjectDoesNotExist',\n    'signals',\n    'CASCADE',\n    'DO_NOTHING',\n    # etc.\n)\n```\n\nThen they can remove the `# noqa` comments for things they're importing but not using. As for the `import *`s this won't help.\n\nWe're planning a different feature that looks a little more like what flake8-putty allows you to do (having a config file with ignore codes per-file). That makes it easier to see at a glance which files are doing making up their own style-guides.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/PyCQA/flake8/issues/comments/812779075/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"asottile","id":1810591,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MTA1OTE=","avatar_u